IMPORT prelude

-- Explosives Act 1961 (Cth) — THE NOUNS, THE RULES AND THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/C1961A00065.txt (compilation No. 9, 11
-- December 2024). The person handling explosives, or entering a Commonwealth
-- explosives area, asks: "Do the Commonwealth's handling rules reach these
-- explosives; if I break the regulations or an order, what is the most I can
-- get?"

§ `Nouns`

-- s 9: whose explosives.
DECLARE `Whose explosives` IS ONE OF
    `the Commonwealth's, or in its possession or control`
    `made by the Commonwealth and being exported under an arrangement with it`
    `a foreign government's or forces', here with Commonwealth approval for defence`
    `anyone else's`

DECLARE `Explosives case` HAS
    `whose explosives`                                      IS A `Whose explosives`
    -- s 20
    `I contravened the regulations or an order`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `days a continuing offence continues`           IS A NUMBER
    `the regulations prescribe a lesser penalty`            IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Explosives position` HAS
    `Part II reaches these explosives`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `I commit an offence`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `maximum imprisonment in months`                        IS A NUMBER
    `maximum fine in penalty units`                         IS A NUMBER
    `a lesser prescribed penalty applies instead`           IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Rules`

@ref s 9
GIVEN c IS A `Explosives case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part II applies` c IF
    NOT (c's `whose explosives` EQUALS `anyone else's`)

-- s 20(a): imprisonment up to 6 months or a fine up to 10 penalty units, or
-- both, and for a continuing offence up to 2 penalty units for each day it
-- continues; (b) or a lesser prescribed penalty.
@ref s 20
GIVEN c IS A `Explosives case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum months for` c MEANS
    IF c's `I contravened the regulations or an order` AND NOT (c's `the regulations prescribe a lesser penalty`) THEN 6 ELSE 0

@ref s 20
GIVEN c IS A `Explosives case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum units for` c MEANS
    IF c's `I contravened the regulations or an order` AND NOT (c's `the regulations prescribe a lesser penalty`)
    THEN 10 PLUS 2 TIMES c's `days a continuing offence continues`
    ELSE 0

@ref ss 9, 20
@export default The position of a person who handles explosives, or is in or near a Commonwealth explosives area, under the Explosives Act 1961 (Cth): whether the Commonwealth's handling regulations (Part II) reach the explosives (Commonwealth explosives, Commonwealth-made explosives being exported under an arrangement, and foreign forces' explosives here with approval for defence: s 9); and, for contravening the regulations or an order made under them, the most that can be imposed (s 20: 6 months' imprisonment or 10 penalty units or both, plus 2 penalty units a day for a continuing offence, unless a lesser penalty is prescribed). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Explosives case`  @desc Whose explosives, whether I contravened the regulations or an order, how many days it continued, and any lesser prescribed penalty
GIVETH A `Explosives position`
`the explosives position for` c MEANS
    `Explosives position` OF `Part II applies` c, c's `I contravened the regulations or an order`, `the maximum months for` c, `the maximum units for` c,
                             c's `I contravened the regulations or an order` AND c's `the regulations prescribe a lesser penalty`
